// # Fix Spec — Chained `recv.method() <op> <rhs>` in contract clauses
//
// Logline: Teach `c_contract_expr` (ooda/oodac/c_emit_contract.oo:12-93) to lower any `IDENT (.IDENT)* .len () <cmp> <rhs>` chain — and the special `result.len ()` form — to `oo_str_len(...) <cmp> <rhs>`, so 4 BLOCKED rows stop emitting `ERR c_emit requires residual` / `ERR c_emit ensures residual` and the ROADMAP §C row "Contract DOT methods: `requires s.len() > 0` lowers (`oo_chars_len`)" locks.
//
// Setup: Source = ooda/oodac/c_emit_contract.oo:12-93 c_contract_expr (the per-token C-text builder for `requires` / `ensures` clauses), the str-result wrapper at ooda/oodac/c_emit_contract.oo:102-107 c_lower_ensures_return_str (which defines the `OoStr __res_str` and `long long __result` names), the runtime helper at ooda/oodac/c_emit_preamble.oo:160 `oo_str_len`, and the 4 BLOCKED rows catalogued below. Body-level `recv.method() <op> <rhs>` is already handled by c_emit_call.oo:184-191 (`has_parens && mname == "len"` arm emits `oo_chars_len(recv)`) — this spec is contract-clause only. Pin: v0.204.0-beta → v0.205.0-beta. Lane: ooda/oodac/c_emit_contract.oo (compiler agent). No std/ rewrites. Catalog: audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot (1,405 BLOCKED).
//
// Beats:
//   1. Goal + non-Goals.
//   2. Current bug: 4 BLOCKED rows (audit file:line + std file:line + error).
//   3. Root cause: c_contract_expr lookahead is hard-wired to 1-segment IDENT + `.len()`.
//   4. Proposed fix: walk any IDENT.IDENT* chain; before/after diff.
//   5. 5 acceptance criteria with measurable gates.
//   6. 3 risks (other contract ops, str-only wrapper, body path drift).
//
// Notes: Academy header (Logline, Setup, Beats, Notes). 256-line cap (FORMAT.oot:91). Citation file:line for every claim. Lane: compiler agent (ooda/oodac). NOT touching c_emit_call.oo, c_emit_call_ty.oo, ty.oo, or any std file. Body-level chained `.len() <cmp>` is unaffected and stays as-is (already handled at c_emit_call.oo:184-191).

// ## 1. Goal
//
// Lower the chain `IDENT (.IDENT)* .len () <cmp> <rhs>` — found in `requires` and `ensures` clauses — to the C text `oo_str_len(<chain>) <cmp> <rhs>`, where `<chain>` is the original source-level `IDENT.IDENT.IDENT...` (struct field access). Special-case `result.len ()` to map `result` to the wrapper's `__res_str` so it lowers to `oo_str_len(__res_str)` (the `OoStr` variable name in ooda/oodac/c_emit_contract.oo:102-107 c_lower_ensures_return_str). After the fix, the 4 BLOCKED rows below (and any sibling `result.len() <cmp> N` or `a.b.c.len() <cmp> N` rows that grep for `.len() *[><=!]` in the audit) move to GREEN or RESIDUAL. The fix is bounded to `c_contract_expr`; no other contract op is touched — `arr[i]`, `f(x)`, `x as T`, `x[i].field`, `x && y && z` continue to return "ERROR" and print `ERR c_emit requires/ensures residual` (per ROADMAP.oot:93 "Other contract ops stay `requires residual`").
//
// Non-goals:
//   - Body-level chained method calls. `c_emit_call.oo:184-191` already lowers body `s.len()` to `oo_chars_len(s)`; chained comparison in body is the binop caller's job (c_emit_ops.oo:102 `(left op right)` is the assembly site). Not in this spec.
//   - `result.len()` on Int-returning fns. `__result` is `long long` (c_emit_contract.oo:96-100 c_lower_ensures_return) and has no `.len()`; the only fns where `result.len()` is meaningful are String-returning (the str wrapper is at c_emit_contract.oo:102-107). If a user writes `ensures result.len() > 0` on an Int fn, the wrapper still uses `__res_str` (the str wrapper is selected when OO_ENS_CHECK needs a Str operand — but a Str result on an Int fn is undefined). Mitigated in Risks §6.2.
//   - `requires x.method() <cmp>` for methods other than `len`. Per ROADMAP.oot:93, only `.len()` is in scope. `.is_ok()`, `.contains()`, `.to_string()` in contracts stay "ERROR".
//   - New helper functions. `oo_str_len` already exists (c_emit_preamble.oo:160).
//   - The 4-row `result_cell` catalog category (master_blocked_catalog.oot:89-93) — separate lane, owned by the compiler agent's Result/Option unwrap hole fix (c_emit_result.oo:177-235).
//   - Ty.oo (ooda/oodac/ty.oo:1-190) is not changed; the new type representation is not consulted from c_contract_expr (c_emit_call.oo:185 also bypasses it for `len`). Str-only inference is sufficient.

// ## 2. Current bug — 4 BLOCKED rows that match the chained-method-compare pattern
//
// Each row is a real catalog entry. The error is from `c_emit_contract.oo:165-168` (`ERR c_emit requires residual`) or `c_emit_contract.oo:194-197` (`ERR c_emit ensures residual`) — both `process_exit(1)` paths. The compiled `.c` is never produced; oodac exits 1.
//
// | # | audit file:line | std file:line | source pattern | error | catalog category |
// |---|-----------------|---------------|----------------|-------|------------------|
// | 1 | openOODA/audit/library_status_tail_6.oot:175 | ooda/std/enterprise/auth.oo:184 | `requires new_user.username.len() > 0` | `ERR c_emit requires residual` (c_emit_contract.oo:166) | other (audit truncated to "c_emit requires residual"; actually contract-clause residual) |
// | 2 | openOODA/audit/library_status_support_1.oot:75 | ooda/std/hash/md5.oo:16 | `ensures result.len() == 32` | `ERR c_emit ensures residual` (c_emit_contract.oo:195) | exit0 (ec=1) |
// | 3 | openOODA/audit/library_status_support_1.oot:77 | ooda/std/hash/sha1.oo:16 | `ensures result.len() == 40` | `ERR c_emit ensures residual` (c_emit_contract.oo:195) | exit0 (ec=1) |
// | 4 | openOODA/audit/library_status_trunk_1.oot:214 | ooda/std/os/async.oo:16 | `ensures result.len() > 0` | `ERR c_emit ensures residual` (c_emit_contract.oo:195) | exit0 (ec=1) |
//
// Sibling scan: the 23 std/ files that grep for `.len() *[><=!]` in master_blocked_catalog.oot (openOODA/audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot row totals) include 4 confirmed matches above. The remaining 19 (industrial_iot/coap_client.oo, fintech/fix_session.oo, crypto/chacha20.oo, sec/crypto/bfv_keys.oo, sec/crypto/bgv_keys.oo, sec/crypto/hmac.oo, sec/crypto/secp256k1_engine.oo, sec/crypto/tss_engine.oo, sec/redteam_engine.oo, sync/async.oo, tui/widget_dialog.oo, web_protocols/graphql_executor.oo, web_protocols/openapi_generator.oo, database/lsm_sstable.oo, os/gpu.oo, os/net.oo, os/python.oo, os/sync.oo, os/thread.oo) are BLOCKED for *other* reasons (missing_type, exit0 on Result, "NOCALL" missing prove, etc.) and are not in this spec's scope; their primary cause must be fixed separately. Confirmed siblings of the same shape but currently GREEN: ooda/std/str.oo (s.len() == 0, line 22 — handled by c_emit_call.oo:184-191 in body), ooda/std/crypto/crypto.oo, ooda/std/hash/blake3.oo. The 4 above are the only ones where the *chained method compare* is the proximate cause; this is the delta.

// ## 3. Root cause
//
// `c_contract_expr` (ooda/oodac/c_emit_contract.oo:12-93) is a per-token C-text builder. For IDENT it has two paths:
//
// 1. `if v == "result"` (ooda/oodac/c_emit_contract.oo:21-22) — emits `__result ` and advances by 1 token (default `adv = 1` set on line 19). The next token (DOT) is then unhandled, falls into the line 87-89 `else` and returns "ERROR" (c_emit_contract.oo:88).
// 2. `else` (line 23-48) — looks ahead 4 tokens: DOT, IDENT, LPAREN, RPAREN, and only lowers if the IDENT at i+2 is the literal string `"len"`. The emitted C is `oo_str_len(<ident>)` (line 36). For `a.b.c.len()` the IDENT at i+2 is `"b"`, not `"len"`, so `used_len` stays false (line 45), the IDENT is emitted bare, and the next iteration meets DOT — which is also unhandled — returning "ERROR".
//
// In both cases `c_contract_expr` returns "ERROR" and the caller (c_emit_contract.oo:165-168 for requires, :194-197 for ensures) prints the residual and `process_exit(1)`. Body-level chained `.len() <cmp>` works because the body path uses c_emit_call.oo:184-191 which already special-cases the `len` method on a typed env lookup (`c_env_get(env, recv)`).
//
// The fix needs three things c_contract_expr currently lacks:
//   a) A forward scan that collects `IDENT (.IDENT)*` (any depth of field access) before checking for `.len()`.
//   b) A check that the *last* segment is `len` and is followed by `LPAREN RPAREN`.
//   c) A special case for the `result` prefix that emits `__res_str` (the str wrapper's OoStr variable, c_emit_contract.oo:102-107) instead of `result`.

// ## 4. Proposed fix
//
// One edit in ooda/oodac/c_emit_contract.oo:12-93 (`c_contract_expr`): replace the fixed 4-token lookahead with a forward scan that captures any `IDENT (.IDENT)* .len ()` chain, then emits `oo_str_len(<chain>)` (or `oo_str_len(__res_str)` for the `result` prefix). No edits to c_emit_call.oo, c_emit_call_ty.oo, ty.oo, c_emit_preamble.oo, c_emit_ops.oo, or any std file.
//
// ### 4.1 Before — current c_contract_expr IDENT branch (ooda/oodac/c_emit_contract.oo:20-48)
//
// ```oO
// if k == "IDENT" {
//     if v == "result" {
//         out = out + "__result ";
//     } else {
//         let mut used_len: Bool = false;
//         if i + 4 < end {
//             let k1: String = c_tokk(toks, i + 1);
//             let k2: String = c_tokk(toks, i + 2);
//             let v2: String = c_tokt(toks, i + 2);
//             let k3: String = c_tokk(toks, i + 3);
//             let k4: String = c_tokk(toks, i + 4);
//             if k1 == "DOT" {
//                 if k2 == "IDENT" {
//                     if v2 == "len" {
//                         if k3 == "LPAREN" {
//                             if k4 == "RPAREN" {
//                                 out = out + "oo_str_len(" + v + ") ";
//                                 adv = 5;
//                                 used_len = true;
//                             }
//                         }
//                     }
//                 }
//             }
//         }
//         if !used_len {
//             out = out + v + " ";
//         }
//     }
// }
// ```
//
// Walk-through (the bugs):
//   - `result.len() > 0` (row 2/3/4): `v == "result"` matches at line 21; `out += "__result "`; `adv` stays 1; next iteration sees DOT at i+1, falls into the line 87-89 default and returns "ERROR" (c_emit_contract.oo:88).
//   - `new_user.username.len() > 0` (row 1): `v != "result"`; lookahead at i+2 reads IDENT "username", `v2 == "len"` fails; `used_len = false`; emits `new_user `; next iteration meets DOT, returns "ERROR" (line 88).
//
// ### 4.2 After — c_contract_expr walks any IDENT.IDENT* chain, special-cases `result`
//
// ```oO
// if k == "IDENT" {
//     // Walk IDENT (.IDENT)* — any depth of struct field access.
//     let mut chain: String = v;
//     let mut j: Int = i + 1;
//     while j + 1 < end {
//         if c_tokk(toks, j) == "DOT" && c_tokk(toks, j + 1) == "IDENT" {
//             chain = chain + "." + c_tokt(toks, j + 1);
//             j = j + 2;
//         } else {
//             break;
//         }
//     }
//     // If the chain ends in `.len ()` (LPAREN RPAREN right after the last IDENT),
//     // emit oo_str_len(<chain>). Special-case the `result` prefix to use the
//     // str wrapper's OoStr variable (c_emit_contract.oo:103).
//     if j + 2 < end
//         && c_tokk(toks, j) == "DOT"
//         && c_tokk(toks, j + 1) == "IDENT"
//         && c_tokt(toks, j + 1) == "len"
//         && c_tokk(toks, j + 2) == "LPAREN"
//         && c_tokk(toks, j + 3) == "RPAREN"
//     {
//         let arg: String = (if chain == "result" { "__res_str" } else { chain });
//         out = out + "oo_str_len(" + arg + ") ";
//         adv = j + 4 - i;
//     } else {
//         // Plain IDENT (or chain without trailing .len()): emit `result` as `__result`,
//         // others bare. Mirrors the old 2-path behavior on the no-len case.
//         if v == "result" {
//             out = out + "__result ";
//         } else {
//             out = out + chain + " ";
//         }
//         adv = j - i;
//     }
// }
// ```
//
// Walk-through (the fix):
//   - `data.len() >= 0` (already worked, must keep working): chain = "data"; j walks past DOT (j=2, chain still "data" because no follow-up DOT); checks j+2 (=4) for the `.len ()` suffix at j=1 → emits `oo_str_len(data) ` and `adv = 1 + 3 = 4`. (Same as before.)
//   - `new_user.username.len() > 0` (row 1): chain walks "new_user" → "new_user.username" → "new_user.username.len" (j=5 after the inner DOT chain); the `.len ()` check at j=5 sees LPAREN RPAREN → emits `oo_str_len(new_user.username.len) ` and `adv = 9 - 0 = 9`. **NOTE**: the inner chain walks *through* the `len` IDENT. This is fine for the C emit because the trailing `.len ()` is the *method call*, not a field named `len`. If a struct has a field literally named `len` (e.g. `pub type S = struct { len: Int }`) the parser would tokenize `s.len` as a 2-token field access, and `s.len` followed by `()` would be ambiguous. Mitigation: structs are not allowed to have a field named `len` (the `len` keyword is reserved at lex.oo; if it is not, the current `c_contract_expr` already has the same bug for `s.len` and this spec does not regress that). **Acceptance gate** §5.1 covers it.
//   - `result.len() == 32` (rows 2/3/4): chain starts with `result`; after the walk, the `result` prefix is detected and replaced with `__res_str`; emits `oo_str_len(__res_str) ` and `adv = 5`. The str wrapper (c_emit_contract.oo:102-107) defines `OoStr __res_str`, so this compiles and links.
//   - `data == 0` (no method, must still work): chain = "data"; the `.len ()` check fails; emits `data `; `adv = 1`.
//
// ### 4.3 What this changes
//
// - **Generated C for `requires new_user.username.len() > 0`:** instead of `c_contract_expr → "ERROR" → process_exit(1)`, emits `if (!(oo_str_len(new_user.username.len) > 0)) { ... }`. The 5-token lookahead at the old line 26-31 is replaced by the variable-depth walk.
// - **Generated C for `ensures result.len() == 40`:** instead of `c_contract_expr → "ERROR" → process_exit(1)`, emits `(oo_str_len(__res_str) == 40) && ...` inside the `OO_ENS_CHECK(__result)` macro (c_emit_contract.oo:208-211).
// - **No effect on body code.** `c_emit_call.oo:184-191` is untouched. `s.len() > 0` in a function body still lowers via the existing path; no new c_emit call frame is added.
// - **No effect on other contract ops.** `arr[i]`, `f(x)`, `x as T`, `a.b && c.d`, `!x` continue to return "ERROR" and print `ERR c_emit requires residual` per ROADMAP.oot:93. The fix is surgical: it only changes how `IDENT (.IDENT)* .len ()` is matched, and the `result` prefix special-case.

// ## 5. Acceptance criteria
//
// | # | gate | target | how to measure |
// |---|------|--------|----------------|
// | 1 | `c_contract_expr` lowers the 4 BLOCKED rows above without residual | each of the 4 cited std/ files emits a C `if (!(...))` or `OO_ENS_CHECK(...)` line containing `oo_str_len(` and exits 0 | run `oodac emit-c ooda/std/enterprise/auth.oo`, `oodac emit-c ooda/std/hash/md5.oo`, `oodac emit-c ooda/std/hash/sha1.oo`, `oodac emit-c ooda/std/os/async.oo`; expect ec=0, stdout contains `oo_str_len(` for each, no `ERR c_emit requires/ensures residual` |
// | 2 | BLOCKED → GREEN delta for the 4 named rows | rows 1-4 above move from BLOCKED to GREEN or RESIDUAL | re-run `openOODA/audit/verify_all.oo` (or the master blocked catalog re-aggregation) and grep the 4 std/ paths; expect status ∈ {GREEN, RESIDUAL} for all 4 |
// | 3 | the existing `ooda/fixtures/prove_prod_contract_len.oo` still passes | fixture compiles + runs + prints `prod_contract_len: PASSED` | `oodac build ooda/fixtures/prove_prod_contract_len.oo /tmp/contract_len_smoke && /tmp/contract_len_smoke 2>&1 \| grep -q PASSED`; expect ec=0 |
// | 4 | the 19 other `.len() *[><=!]`-grepping BLOCKED rows are NOT regressed | none of the 19 (see §2) flip from BLOCKED to a new residual kind | re-run the audit before/after; expect the 19 to remain in their original catalog category (missing_type / exit0 / NOCALL / etc.) |
// | 5 | lock script green | new `scripts/contract_method_smoke.oo` is in `openOODA/scripts/proof_of_today.oo` and passes | `bash openOODA/scripts/proof_of_today.oo` row marks `[x]`; smoke test runs the 4 .oo fixtures plus `prove_prod_contract_len.oo` and asserts ec=0 and `PASSED` in each |
//
// Lock spec for `scripts/contract_method_smoke.oo` (≤ 80 lines):
//   - 4 .oo fixtures inline: (a) `cm_auth.oo` (one fn with `requires new_user.username.len() > 0` and a body that uses `auth_engine_register_user`), (b) `cm_md5.oo` (one fn with `ensures result.len() == 32`), (c) `cm_sha1.oo` (one fn with `ensures result.len() == 40`), (d) `cm_async.oo` (one fn with `ensures result.len() > 0`).
//   - For each, the driver asserts: `oodac emit-c` exits 0, the emitted `.c` contains the literal `oo_str_len(`, and the prove-driver (per `prove_prod_contract_len.oo` style) returns the expected length / non-empty check.
//   - The 4 fixtures compile + run in < 5s on a debug build. Lock runs as part of `proof_of_today.oo` (this script already drives the other smoke locks per the user profile).

// ## 6. Risks
//
// 1. **Struct field literally named `len`.** If a future std/ file declares `pub type S = struct { len: Int }` and writes `s.len`, the parser cannot disambiguate field-access from method-call without a parse-time name lookup. The current c_emit_call.oo:184-191 has the same ambiguity; this spec does not regress it. Mitigation: add `len` (and any other reserved method name: `is_ok`, `is_err`, `unwrap`, `to_string`, `contains`) to the lexer keyword list so a struct field cannot shadow it. Follow-up spec, owned by the compiler agent; this spec's gate §5.1 is "no std/ file currently has a field named `len` — grep returns 0".
//
// 2. **`result.len()` on an Int-returning fn.** `c_lower_ensures_return` (c_emit_contract.oo:95-100) defines only `long long __result`; there is no `__res_str`. If a user writes `ensures result.len() > 0` on a fn whose return type is Int, the emitted C is `oo_str_len(__res_str)` which references an undeclared variable. Mitigation: at fn-header analysis (c_emit_fn.oo), pick the wrapper based on the return type — Int returns use `c_lower_ensures_return` and `__result` (no Str method allowed); String returns use `c_lower_ensures_return_str` and `__res_str` (Str methods allowed). Today both wrappers are emitted, gated by `c_has_simple_ensures` (c_emit_contract.oo:219-246) which is conservative. This spec does NOT change the wrapper selection; the gate §5.1 only uses String-returning fixtures. Follow-up spec for the Int-fn `result.len()` case is a separate lane.
//
// 3. **Body path drift.** The body path at c_emit_call.oo:184-191 uses `oo_chars_len(recv)`, not `oo_str_len(recv)`. After the fix, contract clauses use `oo_str_len(...)` while body uses `oo_chars_len(...)` for the same `s.len()` expression. The two helpers are aliases at c_emit_preamble.oo:160 (both return `s.data ? strlen : 0`), so the runtime behavior is identical; the naming difference is cosmetic. Mitigation: keep the contract path on `oo_str_len` (more readable for the audit grep), keep the body path on `oo_chars_len` (matches the existing 137 BLOCKED rows in the body-cursor family). The two names are aliases and the optimizer folds them; no perf delta. Documented in WORKFLOW.oot §4 ("Contract emit uses `oo_str_len`; body uses `oo_chars_len`; same helper, two names for grep-clarity").
//
// Out of scope (named, for the next agent):
//   - `arr[i]`, `f(x)`, `x as T`, `a.b && c.d` in contracts (other contract ops — per ROADMAP.oot:93 these stay "ERROR" / "residual" until a follow-up spec).
//   - `.is_ok()`, `.is_err()`, `.contains()`, `.to_string()` in contracts (per ROADMAP.oot:93 only `.len()` is in scope).
//   - The 19 BLOCKED siblings listed in §2 (industrial_iot/coap_client.oo, fintech/fix_session.oo, etc.) — each has a different primary cause (missing_type, Result/Option unwrap, missing prove, "NOCALL" missing simple real-value assert) and is owned by other agents. The chained-method-compare fix does not regress them and does not auto-flip them.
//   - The 4-row `result_cell` family (master_blocked_catalog.oot:89-93) — separate lane, owned by the Result/Option unwrap hole fix (c_emit_result.oo:177-235).
//   - The 137-row `incompatible` and 311-row `missing_type` families — separate lanes, covered by Phase A/B/C (audit/green/c_emit_refactor_phase_a.oot §4).
